course: dictionary
lesson: 10379
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and treble is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «Treble the amount of flour» is a recipe telling you to make it three times bigger, not a voice being high.
explain: Look for clues about the topic. «Many boys sing very high before their voices change; cathedral choirs have high voices called trebles.» Sing, voices and choirs tell you this is about music, so treble means a high singing voice.
explain: Test each meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Prices may treble this year» still makes sense with "become three times as big", but not with "a high singing voice". When one word could fit two meanings, read the whole text before you decide.
fact: Treble can be a verb, an adjective, a noun or a determiner, and its job in the sentence changes its meaning.
fact: «To treble» means to become three times as big, or to make something three times as big.
fact: «Treble» as an adjective or determiner means three times as much, as in «treble the price».
fact: In music, «the treble» is the high part, and a «treble» is a boy with a high singing voice.
fact: «The treble clef» is the sign for high notes, and it is also called the G clef.
exercise: «Treble the amount of flour in the recipe.» What does treble mean here? | Very quiet | A high singing voice | *Three times as much | Half as much
exercise: «Cathedral choirs have high voices called trebles.» What is a treble in this sentence? | A winning trophy | A type of drum | A three-times-bigger price | *A boy with a high singing voice
exercise: «The treble clef is also called the G clef.» Which note does its curl wrap around? | A | F | D | *G
test: «Prices may treble this year.» What does treble mean here? | Become a boy with a high voice | Become half as big | Become very quiet | *Become three times as big
test: In the treble clef, what note is on the top line? | D | G | *F | E
exam: Which meaning fits «The choir's treble sang the top notes»? | A winning trophy | Three times as big | Three times as much money | *A high singing voice
